WEBVTT

00:00:10.671 --> 00:00:12.339
That was thrilling. (giggles)

00:00:12.423 --> 00:00:14.216
How in the world did you end up here?

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.051
I have no idea.

00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:17.761
EDMUND: Caspian.

00:00:18.804 --> 00:00:19.930
Edmund.

00:00:20.014 --> 00:00:21.891
-It's great to see you.
-Good to see you.

00:00:21.974 --> 00:00:23.559
Didn't you call for us?

00:00:23.642 --> 00:00:25.895
No. Not this time.

00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:29.064
Well, whatever the case,
I'm just glad to be here.

00:00:29.148 --> 00:00:30.691
(Eustace screaming)

00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:32.860
Don't touch me!

00:00:32.943 --> 00:00:35.196
Get that thing off me!

00:00:35.279 --> 00:00:37.907
(grunting, panting)

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.408
Reepicheep!

00:00:40.743 --> 00:00:43.037
Oh. Your Majesties.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.206
Hello, Reep. What a pleasure.

00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:47.124
The pleasure is all mine, sir.

00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:51.295
But first, what to do about this...
this... hysterical interloper?

00:00:51.378 --> 00:00:54.715
(coughing) That giant rat thing
just tried to claw my face off!

00:00:54.798 --> 00:00:58.928
I was merely trying to expel
the water from your lungs, sir.

00:00:59.011 --> 00:01:01.388
It talked! Did you see...
anyone just hear that?

00:01:01.472 --> 00:01:03.807
-It... it just talked!
-He always talks.

00:01:03.891 --> 00:01:05.392
Actually, it's getting him
to shut up that's the trick.

00:01:05.476 --> 00:01:07.728
The moment there is nothing
to be said, Your Highness,

00:01:07.811 --> 00:01:10.231
I promise you, I will not say it.

00:01:10.314 --> 00:01:11.982
Look, I don't know
what kind of prank this is,

00:01:12.066 --> 00:01:14.193
but I want to wake up right now!

00:01:14.276 --> 00:01:16.570
Perhaps we could throw him back.

00:01:16.654 --> 00:01:18.739
EUSTACE: ...and kidnapped
by some sort of seafaring carnival!

00:01:18.822 --> 00:01:21.659
-Edmund!
-(crewmen chuckling)

00:01:21.742 --> 00:01:24.328
I demand to know!
Just where in the blazes am I?

00:01:24.411 --> 00:01:28.040
You're on the Dawn Treader,
the finest ship in Narnia's navy.

00:01:28.123 --> 00:01:30.918
-(swooning)
-(men laughing)

00:01:34.088 --> 00:01:35.756
Was it something I said?

00:01:36.966 --> 00:01:38.133
See to him, will you?

00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:39.635
Your Majesty.

00:01:39.718 --> 00:01:42.513
Aw... (chuckles)

00:01:42.596 --> 00:01:43.764
Men...

00:01:45.558 --> 00:01:47.643
Behold our castaways...

00:01:48.936 --> 00:01:51.856
...Edmund the Just
and Lucy the Valiant,

00:01:52.857 --> 00:01:55.526
High King and Queen of Narnia.

00:02:24.805 --> 00:02:26.348
Aslan.

00:02:33.272 --> 00:02:36.942
Look. Susan's bow and arrows.

00:02:37.026 --> 00:02:38.819
Lucy.

00:02:39.945 --> 00:02:43.157
My healing cordial.
And dagger.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.326
Oh. May I?

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:46.827
Of course. They're yours.

00:02:46.911 --> 00:02:49.038
-Peter's sword.
-Yes.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.582
I looked after it as promised.

00:02:53.876 --> 00:02:55.836
Here. Hold it if you wish.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.671
No, no. It's yours.

00:02:58.255 --> 00:02:59.882
Peter gave it to you.

00:03:01.008 --> 00:03:03.302
I did save this for you, though.

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:10.059
Thanks.

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:14.146
CASPIAN: Since you left us,
the Giants of the North

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:15.773
have surrendered unconditionally.

00:03:15.856 --> 00:03:18.025
And we defeated the Calormen
armies at the Great Desert.

00:03:18.859 --> 00:03:20.569
There's peace across all of Narnia.

00:03:20.653 --> 00:03:23.322
-Peace?
-In just three years.

00:03:24.031 --> 00:03:26.408
And have you found yourself
a queen in those three years?

00:03:27.284 --> 00:03:30.287
No. Not one to compare
with your sister.

00:03:30.371 --> 00:03:32.373
EDMUND: Hang on.
So if there are no wars to fight

00:03:32.456 --> 00:03:35.751
and no one's in trouble,
then why are we here?

00:03:35.835 --> 00:03:38.671
That's a good question.
I've been asking myself the same thing.

00:03:38.754 --> 00:03:40.506
So where are we sailing to?

00:03:40.589 --> 00:03:43.008
Before I took back the
throne from my uncle,

00:03:43.092 --> 00:03:47.012
he tried to kill my father's closest
friends and most loyal supporters--

00:03:47.096 --> 00:03:49.181
the seven lords of Telmar.

00:03:53.644 --> 00:03:55.187
They fled to the Lone Islands.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.190
No one's heard from them since.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.027
So you think something's
happened to them?

00:04:02.111 --> 00:04:05.823
Well, if it has,
it's my duty to find out.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.910
LUCY: Well, what's east
of the Lone Islands?

00:04:09.994 --> 00:04:11.871
DRINIAN:
Uncharted waters.

00:04:12.746 --> 00:04:14.498
Things you could barely imagine.

00:04:15.457 --> 00:04:17.793
Tales of sea serpents and worse.

00:04:20.212 --> 00:04:21.422
Sea serpents?

00:04:21.505 --> 00:04:24.466
All right, Captain.
That's enough of your tall tales.

00:04:29.847 --> 00:04:31.724
(crewmen shouting commands)

00:04:35.769 --> 00:04:38.397
REEPICHEEP: ♪ Where sky and water meet ♪

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.275
♪ Where the waves grow ever sweet ♪

00:04:41.358 --> 00:04:45.446
♪ Doubt not, you, Reepicheep ♪

00:04:45.529 --> 00:04:48.574
♪ To find all that you seek ♪

00:04:48.657 --> 00:04:51.076
♪ There is the utter East ♪

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.411
-♪ Doubt not... ♪
-LUCY: That's pretty.

00:04:52.494 --> 00:04:55.331
Aah! Ooh! Oh! Thank you.

00:04:55.414 --> 00:04:58.417
A dryad sung it to me
when I was just a mouseling.

00:04:59.293 --> 00:05:02.588
I can't divine the meaning, but, uh,
I've never forgotten the words.

00:05:02.671 --> 00:05:04.882
What do you think is past
the Lone Islands, Reep?

00:05:04.965 --> 00:05:07.885
Well, I've been told
the furthest east one can sail

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:10.596
is to the end of the world--
Aslan's country.

00:05:10.679 --> 00:05:12.848
Do you really believe
there's such a place?

00:05:12.932 --> 00:05:15.893
Well, we have nothing, if not belief.

00:05:18.771 --> 00:05:20.981
So you think you
could actually sail there?

00:05:21.065 --> 00:05:23.776
Well, there is only one way
of finding that out.

00:05:24.485 --> 00:05:26.862
I can only hope I will one day
earn the right to see it.

00:05:26.946 --> 00:05:29.114
(chuckles)
Your Majesty.

